{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955944-flash-glitter-and-scream-what-are-the-most-impressive-powers","id":955944,"title":"Flash, Glitter and Scream - What are the most impressive powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-22T15:53:54-07:00","id":955944,"title":"Flash, Glitter and Scream - What are the most impressive powers?","content":"...I should probably apologize in advance for the title, shouldn't I? Anyway, though the Chronicles of Darkness go out of their way to avoid allowing for the &quot;monstrous superhero&quot; playstyle associated with the World of Darkness, it's not as if every supernatural power is a something that can be easily explained as smoke, mirrors, sleight of hand and tricks of the light. But, I recently found myself curious about just how flashy the supernaturals of the Chronicles can be when they really cut loose - the sorts of things that they can do which can spawn an &quot;oh crap!&quot; from the mortals across the room.<br /> <br /> So, being that my own collection is rather sporadic, I thought I'd turn to the forum for assistance. I want your opinions on the flashiest, lethalist, most grandiose and potentially nightmarish displays of occult power and supernatural might that exist in the arsenals of the player splats of the Chronicles of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Just to be clear, I'm not looking to get into any sort of &quot;whose powers are better&quot; argument here. Everyone knows that there's a difference between a vampire using Protean 5 to become a nightmarish inhuman predator and a Mummy using Tier 3 of... whatever Utterance that is which calls down a meteor strike. But both are suitably crap-your-pants scary that I'd consider them perfect examples of &quot;flashy powers&quot; for the sake of this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T16:25:53-07:00","id":955967,"title":"","content":"With the Gift of the Elementals, a werewolf can expand the area of effect of their Influence to a radius of miles equal to twice their Glory. So with just the Gift of the Elementals you can create fire, water, earth or air within that area and cause it to do, basically, whatever you want through the use of Manipulation, allowing for earthquakes and tornadoes.<br /> <br /> However, fetishes exist as an open-ended method of altering Gift Facets. So with the right fetish you can mix them together and create bizarre things, like mixing Influences of Air and Sharks to create sharknados or Fire and Spiders to create Lavalantulas. Or go conceptual and create a Silencequake or have it rain sunlight.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Had to go when first posting.<br /> <br /> One of my favorites and certainly obvious, though arguably no more obvious than a werewolf just changing into a werewolf, is the Temple of Apollo and their ability to, when on a sacred hunt, become supercharged against certain prey and have Apollo's sunlight pour from their eyes and mouth. Which is the type of eerily horrifying imagery I find all too rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-22-2016, 10:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:06:18-07:00","id":956040,"title":"","content":"Mages are fantastic at this, simply because of how arbitrarily pant-shitting they can make their spells when they don't care about Paradox (or they've reached Archmastery and thus don't have to give a damn). I mean, this is the splat where walking to the deepest part of human gestalt consciousness and ripping stuff out is a valid way of changing public opinion, and calling down lightning and holy fire is low to mid-tier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:18:28-07:00","id":956044,"title":"","content":"The Mummy corebook has an Utterance where your magic goes back to the dawn of time and rewrites the path of an asteroid so that it slams to earth and kills the target in front of you. The highest version of the power expands it to hit everything in a mile radius of yourself.<br /> <br /> There's also one for the Guildmasters of the Deceived where you unmake someone from the universe, and if they have the ability to resurrect themselves they cannot do so for a thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:39:25-07:00","id":956055,"title":"","content":"Honestly, almost every Tier 3 Utterance is great for just showing off. The most useless Utterance (Waters of Life and Death), the only one my players and I could see no reason to take, still lets you turn all water in the area into blood or even just part a body of water for your Moses impression (complete with Burning Bush courtesy of Power of Re).<br /> <br /> When it comes to flashy though, I don't think much tops Secrets Ripped From Skies as even the OP has pointed out. My personal favourite runner up is one of the &quot;Words of Dead something&quot; Utterances (Words of Dead Hunger?) which summons something that is a shoggoth in what is basically all but name.<br /> <br /> If anything were to top these Utterances though, I would say it would be a five dot Seba. Those that exist are of truly cosmic significance. If one can wake every Mummy in the world at once at Sekhem 10, how spectacular a display could something of similar power conjure up were it to have a more directly visual impact?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:56:20-07:00","id":956064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955944-flash-glitter-and-scream-what-are-the-most-impressive-powers?p=956055#post956055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, almost every Tier 3 Utterance is great for just showing off. The most useless Utterance (Waters of Life and Death), the only one my players and I could see no reason to take, still lets you turn all water in the area into blood or even just part a body of water for your Moses impression (complete with Burning Bush courtesy of Power of Re).<br /> <br /> When it comes to flashy though, I don't think much tops Secrets Ripped From Skies as even the OP has pointed out. My personal favourite runner up is one of the &amp;quot;Words of Dead something&amp;quot; Utterances (Words of Dead Hunger?) which summons something that is a shoggoth in what is basically all but name.<br /> <br /> If anything were to top these Utterances though, I would say it would be a five dot Seba. Those that exist are of truly cosmic significance. If one can wake every Mummy in the world at once at Sekhem 10, how spectacular a display could something of similar power conjure up were it to have a more directly visual impact?</div> </div> </div> </div>While less stunning than Secrets Ripped From Skies, there's a special spot in my heart for Ancestry of Forgotten Stars. You and your closest friends form a terrifying eldritch flesh Voltron and possibly summon Nyarlathotep as an unexpected side effect!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:39:49-07:00","id":956086,"title":"","content":"Beasts can get pretty nuts, especially at the Incarnate level. Cyclopean Strength scales off Size, theoretically allowing a Beast with that and Looming Presence to lift objects up to almost Size 400. Which is... considerably larger than any man made structure, that's whole mountains. Even at Lair 3 they can be throwing 18 wheelers around. <br /> <br /> Looming Presence also adds a shit ton of health, to the point where that same Incarnate could take a depleted uranium tank buster round to the chest and keep going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T20:11:25-07:00","id":956104,"title":"","content":"Demon: Rain of Blood. Combine with practically any other Embed or Exploit in a Lambda (or when an Analyst Goes Loud), and it's even worse. Hellfire Rain? Turn everything in the area into Cryptids? Make everyone Hate everyone else (or just one person)? The sky is the limit (pun intended).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T23:35:47-07:00","id":956181,"title":"","content":"I always thought that Demon's &quot;Show of Power&quot; was conceptually impressive. Here you have an ability that you can literally mimic anything magical that you've seen before. It's the perfect confluence of memory, blending in with others and sheer ridiculousness that it stands out in my mind. A Demon with Show of Power has literally faked it so hard that they've made it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:16:41-07:00","id":967142,"title":"","content":"You know, I was actually about to start up a thread asking for people to submit their ideas for feats of magical might that a Storyteller who favors a more &quot;Humanity is Insignificant&quot; flavor of Cosmic Horror to their Mortals games could use to emphasize &quot;this is why the Supernatural is SCARY and you should be afraid&quot;... but, that'd basically be repeating this thread, wouldn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:49:42-07:00","id":970594,"title":"","content":"Renowned Bodhisattva Predators capable of spontaneous volcanic eruptions, alludes, basically every Syfy cheesy movie plot you could imagine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:30:39-07:00","id":970620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955944-flash-glitter-and-scream-what-are-the-most-impressive-powers?p=956104#post956104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon: Rain of Blood. Combine with practically any other Embed or Exploit in a Lambda (or when an Analyst Goes Loud), and it's even worse. Hellfire Rain? Turn everything in the area into Cryptids? Make everyone Hate everyone else (or just one person)? The sky is the limit (pun intended).</div> </div> </div> </div>Important note: For maximum effect, Go Loud first. That a)amps up Rain of Blood, b)guarantees you have enough power to use it and c)guarantees you have access to Rain of Blood even if you normally don't have it.<br /> <br /> That's right, every demon can set off a tacnuke at any time. All they need is a Cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:41:20-07:00","id":970652,"title":"","content":"A 2e Changeling can effectively use Animate Device to Kit of Night Rider fame. Or send the Statue of Liberty ramaging through New York City.<br /> <br /> Hedgewall can alliw to create a giant Hedge Castle out doors (it gets weirder when one realizes the Hedge is not always literally a Hedge).<br /> <br /> Phantom Glory with the Elemental Seeming effect + Embracing the Wyrd + Wyrd 10. You turn into something like the human touch, are immune to all mundane weapons, can walk through walls, deal elemental damage to your target which you can massively enhance the die pool thanks to Embracing the Wyrd, and if you get an exceptional success on contract activation you can make someone else like that too. Oh and can bewitch people with Embracing the Wyrd.<br /> <br /> Using Chrysalis you can turn into any animal or object, including of massive size, with extra weapons and possibly weirder stuff. Add Embrace the Wyrd and the Colossus Kith Blessing for more fun.<br /> <br /> Bedlam at 10 Wyrd, you can incite a riot, orgy, paniac, ect... in everyone within 100 yards (the size of a football field), add Embrace the Wyrd to make it nearly impossible to resist, including inducing orgies at funerals or abject terror during the Christmas parade.<br /> <br /> Vainglory is designed spefically to be flashy its in the name.<br /> <br /> For Prommies, causing a Firestorm.<br /> <br /> Vampires Majesty 5.<br /> <br /> Using Cruac 5 to create a Blood God.<br /> <br /> Walkong up a pissed off Mummy, just the sight of them rising from their tomb from the dead.<br /> <br /> A Werewolf in war form of raging.<br /> <br /> Demon burning cover.<br /> <br /> Deviant blowing out.<br /> <br /> True Fae, period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T08:19:15-07:00","id":970709,"title":"","content":"The Strix have a power (Labyrinth, I think?) that lets them selectively delete doors from an arbitrarily large structure.<br /> <br /> Idigam can pick stuff up like &quot;wildlife within a few miles becomes twisted and hateful&quot; as a <i>passive</i> ability.<br /> <br /> =---=<br /> <br /> Speaking of flashy - 3rd Edition D&amp;D had a sourcebook that gave you 5~7 cosmic-horror style campaigns. The one thing that I want to steal and port from that are <i>Signs</i>, which are stuff like &quot;the stars are wrong&quot;, &quot;life runs <i>utterly</i> rampant&quot;, &quot;temperatures start dropping <i>way</i> too fast&quot;, or (to bring in some fan-made ones) &quot;our whole language has become suspect to itself&quot; and &quot;your senses become more and more <i>useless</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Note: these are all <i>global scale</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T09:56:08-07:00","id":970756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/955944-flash-glitter-and-scream-what-are-the-most-impressive-powers?p=970709#post970709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idigam can pick stuff up like &quot;wildlife within a few miles becomes twisted and hateful&quot; as a <i>passive</i> ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. That's a mix between Crazed Evolution, which twists animals into something closer to the idigam and Mad Fecundity, which does the hateful part. When paired they're likely especially nasty.<br /> <br /> 'The idigam\u2019s mere presence causes the natural world to rise up in revolt. Plants erupt into growth and overwhelm buildings in mere hours, while animals become ferocious and aggressive. Creatures of all kinds become incredibly fecund and fertile, often accompanied by murderous levels of territoriality and competitiveness. Each hour that the idigam is present in an area of radius equal to its Rank in miles, all stationary mechanical objects and artificial structures suffer one point of Structure damage as vines wrap them, mold blooms amidst their workings, and concrete shatters from rising roots. Animals are aggressive to all human beings, Uratha, and supernatural beings. Any attempts to influence them \u2014 including supernatural powers \u2014 suffer a penalty equal to the idigam\u2019s Rank.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}